<title>USA: Caremark gets 3-year $500 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Caremark gets 3-year $500 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caremark Inc said Tuesday it finalized a three-year contract to provide and manage all aspects of the mail service and retail prescription drug benefits for the National Association of Letter Carriers 175,000 active and retired members.</p>
<p>The agreement is a valued at about $500 million.</p>
<p>Caremark provides prescription benefit, disease management, and international health care services to individuals, corporations, unions, federal and state agencies, insurance companies and HMOs. It is is a wholly owned subsidiary of MedPartners Inc, a large physician practice management company.</p>
